{
  "$comment": [
    "Cross-language conformance table for the GEH statistic (unit 1.5, D2).",
    "ONE source of truth consumed by BOTH runtimes so the Python and TypeScript",
    "implementations can never drift silently:",
    "  Python -> backend/tests/test_geh_conformance.py  (services.validation)",
    "  TS     -> frontend/tests/geh-conformance.test.ts (frontend/lib/geh.ts)",
    "Semantics pinned here (D1): null when either input is null; null when",
    "either input is NON-FINITE; null when model + observed <= 0; null when the",
    "result overflows to non-finite; otherwise",
    "sqrt(2*(model-observed)^2/(model+observed)), UNROUNDED at the source.",
    "grade: good <5, fair <10, poor otherwise, null when geh is null.",
    "Add a case here before changing either implementation.",
    "",
    "NON-FINITE SENTINELS: JSON cannot encode NaN or Infinity, which is why the",
    "two implementations were able to diverge on exactly those inputs while this",
    "fixture stayed green. Any numeric slot may therefore carry the STRING",
    "\"NaN\", \"Infinity\" or \"-Infinity\"; both readers decode those three",
    "spellings (and only those three -- an unknown string must raise, never be",
    "silently skipped). Applies to case.model, case.observed, case.geh and every",
    "entry of pass_rate_cases.values."
  ],
  "non_finite_sentinels": [
    "NaN",
    "Infinity",
    "-Infinity"
  ],
  "tolerance": 1e-12,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "exact match",
      "model": 500,
      "observed": 500,
      "geh": 0.0,
      "grade": "good"
    },
    {
      "name": "small deviation stays in the good band",
      "model": 510,
      "observed": 500,
      "geh": 0.4449941594899848,
      "grade": "good"
    },
    {
      "name": "fair band",
      "model": 1200,
      "observed": 1000,
      "geh": 6.030226891555273,
      "grade": "fair"
    },
    {
      "name": "poor band",
      "model": 1200,
      "observed": 800,
      "geh": 12.649110640673518,
      "grade": "poor"
    },
    {
      "name": "band edge just under 5",
      "model": 1104,
      "observed": 1000,
      "geh": 3.206457363086679,
      "grade": "good"
    },
    {
